            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 20,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "what-is-an-origin",
      "heading": "What is an Origin?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "text": "An origin is defined by the scheme, host, and port of a URL."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 13,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "URL",
                "Origin Components"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "https://example.com:443/page",
                  "scheme=https, host=example.com, port=443"
                ],
                [
                  "http://example.com:80/page",
                  "scheme=http, host=example.com, port=80"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cross-origin-definition",
          "heading": "Cross-Origin Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "blockquote",
              "text": "Two URLs are considered cross-origin if any one of the scheme, host, or port is different."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 16,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "why-block-cross-origin-requests",
      "heading": "Why Block Cross-Origin Requests?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Security measure to enforce the Same-Origin Policy.",
            "Prevents malicious scripts from accessing sensitive data from another origin."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 17,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "without-cors",
          "heading": "Without CORS:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If a script from https://abc.com tries to fetch resources from https://xyz.com, it results in a CORS error like:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "Access to fetch at 'https://xyz.com/api/data' from origin 'https://abc.com' has been blocked by CORS policy.",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 18,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "what-is-cors",
      "heading": "What is CORS?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "text": "CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) is a mechanism that allows servers to specify who can access resources from different origins."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Implemented via HTTP headers sent by the server.",
            "Tells the browser which origins are permitted to access resources."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 37,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "enabling-cors-in-a-spring-rest-application",
      "heading": "Enabling CORS in a Spring REST Application",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring provides three levels to enable CORS:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Method-Level CORS Configuration",
            "Class-Level CORS Configuration",
            "Global (Application-Level) CORS Configuration"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 17,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "method-level",
      "heading": "Method-Level",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Use the @CrossOrigin annotation on a specific handler method."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@GetMapping(\"/data\")\n@CrossOrigin(origins = \"https://abc.com\")\npublic List<Data> getData() {\n    return dataService.getAllData();\n}",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Customization Options (Annotation Attributes):"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attribute",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "origins",
              "Specifies allowed origins"
            ],
            [
              "methods",
              "Specifies allowed HTTP methods"
            ],
            [
              "allowedHeaders",
              "Allowed headers in request"
            ],
            [
              "exposedHeaders",
              "Headers exposed to client"
            ],
            [
              "allowCredentials",
              "Whether credentials are allowed"
            ],
            [
              "maxAge",
              "Caching duration (in seconds) of preflight request response"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 48,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "class-level",
      "heading": "Class-Level",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Apply @CrossOrigin at the class level to enable CORS for all handler methods in a controller."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/api\")\n@CrossOrigin(origins = \"https://abc.com\", methods = {RequestMethod.GET, RequestMethod.POST})\npublic class MyController {\n    // All endpoints here support cross-origin requests\n    \n}",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 16,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "global-application-level",
      "heading": "Global (Application-Level)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Define CORS globally for the whole application using WebMvcConfigurer."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Configuration\npublic class CorsConfig implements WebMvcConfigurer {\n    @Override\n    public void addCorsMappings(CorsRegistry registry) {\n        registry.addMapping(\"/**\")  // Apply to all paths\n                .allowedOrigins(\"https://abc.com\")\n                .allowedMethods(\"GET\", \"POST\")\n                .allowedHeaders(\"*\")\n                .allowCredentials(false)\n                .maxAge(3600);\n    }\n}",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Notes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Suitable for centralized, consistent configuration.",
            "Can be overridden locally by method/class-level annotations."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 22,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Same-Origin",
            "Cross-Origin"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Allowed by Default",
              "✅",
              "❌"
            ],
            [
              "Requires CORS Configuration",
              "❌",
              "✅"
            ],
            [
              "Use Case",
              "UI and API in same domain",
              "Separate UI and API"
            ],
            [
              "Mechanism",
              "Not needed",
              "@CrossOrigin or global config"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 32,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "common-cors-issues-solutions",
          "heading": "Common CORS Issues & Solutions",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Issue",
                "Cause",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CORS error in browser",
                  "CORS not enabled on server",
                  "Add appropriate @CrossOrigin or global config"
                ],
                [
                  "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * with credentials",
                  "Wildcard not allowed with allowCredentials=true",
                  "Use specific origin instead of *"
                ],
                [
                  "Preflight request failure",
                  "Server not handling OPTIONS requests properly",
                  "Ensure HTTP OPTIONS is supported and configured"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 49,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cors-security-best-practices",
          "heading": "CORS Security Best Practices",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Best Practice",
                "Reason"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Enable CORS only when needed",
                  "Prevents unnecessary exposure"
                ],
                [
                  "Avoid using wildcard * for Access-Control-Allow-Origin unless for open/public APIs",
                  "Wildcards open access to all domains"
                ],
                [
                  "Use a whitelist of trusted origins",
                  "Restricts access to approved clients"
                ],
                [
                  "Use global CORS config + override locally if needed",
                  "Centralized control with flexibility"
                ],
                [
                  "Avoid allowCredentials=true unless absolutely required",
                  "Increases risk of CSRF"
                ],
                [
                  "Use additional security measures (e.g., tokens, hashing, encryption) when allowing credentials",
                  "Ensures secure data transmission"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 75,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
